    ],
    "text": "Music In\ufb02uence and Evolution Analysis Based on Networks"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000009",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0010-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0002-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u516c\u4f17\u53f7\uff1a\u6570\u5b66\u6a21\u578b"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000",
      "p0001-n0011-l0001",
      "p0001-n0011-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u201cMusic is like a psychiatrist. It will answer you with things people can\u2019t tell you.\u201d said the Beatles, one of the most famous Pop/Rock artist. In this paper, we deeply explore the magic of music - its in\ufb02uence network, evolution path, and effects on the culture."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0000",
      "p0001-n0012-l0001",
      "p0001-n0012-l0002",
      "p0001-n0012-l0003",
      "p0001-n0012-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task 1, we build a directed network between in\ufb02uencers and followers. Based on net- work theory, we proposed three different metrics - Degree Centrality, Weighted Degree Central- ity and Eigen Centrality. Then we develop a combination of these metrics as a comprehensive measure of music in\ufb02uence. After that, we create a subnetwork to illustrate our in\ufb02uence mea- sure."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task 2, we \ufb01rst preprocess the data using Principal Component Analysis to reduce dimension and collinearity. Then we de\ufb01ne and calculate the distance between different tracks to obtain the similarity between artists. By calculating the average similarity, we apply Mann-"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0003-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Whitney test. Results show that with the probability of 62.8% and p-value smaller than 0.001, artists within a genre are more similar than those between genres."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001",
      "p0001-n0014-l0002",
      "p0001-n0014-l0003",
      "p0001-n0014-l0004",
      "p0001-n0014-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task 3, according to proposed music similarity measure, we \ufb01nd that similarities and in\ufb02uences within and between genres differ greatly when we analyse different genres. To dis- tinguish one genre from others, we build a Genre Classi\ufb01cation Tree Model. By analysing the number of in\ufb02uencers in different period, we explore the evolution path of genres. Based on the directed network on genre scale, we \ufb01nd Pop/Rock has a strong relationship with R&B, Blues and Folk."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0015-l0000",
      "p0001-n0015-l0001",
      "p0001-n0015-l0002",
      "p0001-n0015-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task 4, we build a Similarity Bayesian Network to identify the real followers based on the music characterstic similarity in tracks. Then we apply a multivariate two-sample mean test and \ufb01nd there is no strong evidence (p-value > 0.1) that any music characteristic are more \u201ccontagious\u201d than others."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0016-l0000",
      "p0001-n0016-l0001",
      "p0001-n0016-l0002",
      "p0001-n0016-l0003",
      "p0001-n0016-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task 5, we \ufb01rst analyze the rise and decline of genres and \ufb01nd the music revolution in 1950s. We proposed a Dynamic Programming Algorithm to detect change points in music characteristics which are consistent with the revolution. Our results show that acousticness, energy, danceability and loudness might signify revolutions. Based on the Bayesian Network, Elvis Presley and Cliff Richard represent revolutionaires."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0017-l0000",
      "p0001-n0017-l0001",
      "p0001-n0017-l0002",
      "p0001-n0017-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task 6, to get a further insight into the evolution in Pop/Rock, we propose an Dynamic In\ufb02uencer Indicator based on the lagging trend in music characteristics of the whole genre. From 1960s to 2010s, there are 10 dynamic in\ufb02uencers, each has his/her unique in\ufb02uence on the genre. Moreover, we explain the evolution of Pop/Rock."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0018-l0000",
      "p0001-n0018-l0001",
      "p0001-n0018-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task 7, three important periods are detected based on time series analysis, which show the culture-in\ufb02uence of music. Based on the model established, we identify social changes like countercultural movement and technological changes such as the proliferation of the Internet."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000021",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0019-l0000",
      "p0001-n0019-l0001",
      "p0001-n0019-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "At last, we conduct sensitivity analysis, which shows the robustness of our model. We also summerize the stengths and weaknesses and provide insights to ICM society about the evolution and cultural in\ufb02uence of music."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000022",
    "issues": [],
